{"name":"Marble Quarry","hex":"#e2dcd7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A metamorphic rock of crystalline limestone. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A small ball used in games, originally of marble but now usually of glass or ceramic."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (something to have) the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example by mixing viscous ingredients incompletely, or by applying paint or other colorants unevenly.","To get or have the streaked or swirled appearance of certain types of marble, for example due to the incomplete mixing of viscous ingredients, or the uneven application of paint or other colorants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marble"},{"term":"quarry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A site for mining stone, such as limestone, or slate."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To obtain (or mine) stone by extraction from a quarry.","To extract or slowly obtain by long, tedious searching."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quarry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Quarry","blocks":[{"text":"A quarry is a place where rock and earth materials – such as limestone, marble, granite, gravel, and sand – are excavated. The operation of quarries is regulated in some jurisdictions to manage their safety risks and reduce their environmental impact."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/PortlandQuarry.jpg/330px-PortlandQuarry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quarry","wikidata":"Q188040"},{"title":"Marble","blocks":[{"text":"Marble is a metamorphic rock consisting of carbonate minerals (most commonly calcite (CaCO3) or dolomite (CaMg(CO3)2) that have recrystallized under the influence of heat and pressure. It has a crystalline texture, and is typically not foliated (layered), although there are exceptions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Marmo_z17.JPG/330px-Marmo_z17.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marble","wikidata":"Q40861"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG/500px-Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG/1280px-Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG/500px-Stone_quarry_adelaide.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An abandoned construction aggregate quarry near Adelaide, South Australia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStone_quarry_adelaide.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg/1280px-Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg/500px-Sulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An abandoned construction aggregate quarry with turquoise pond near Thouars, France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASulfureuse_vir%C3%A9e.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Stone_Quarry_Kerala.JPG/500px-Stone_Quarry_Kerala.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu